     "body": "<p>I removed the JBoss repo entirely, and added the GlassFish repo as part of addressing \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-961\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-961\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Maven cannot find javax.resource:connector-api\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-961\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n. With a clean Maven repo, I'm not getting any errors retrieving artifacts and the tests all pass. I'm not actually sure what dependency the JBoss repo was originally intended to satisfy.</p>\n\n<p>Marked as fixed as of 20130585a473f64a698d32d5cb915c56043f1c1d.</p>",
