  "description": "<p>The JBoss repository <a href=\"http://repository.jboss.org/maven2\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://repository.jboss.org/maven2</a> is no longer available according to <a href=\"http://community.jboss.org/en/build/blog/2011/06/01/blocking-repositoryjbossorgmaven2\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://community.jboss.org/en/build/blog/2011/06/01/blocking-repositoryjbossorgmaven2</a>. It prevents to build the fcrepo project in case necessary dependencies were not already available in local .m2 repository.</p>\n\n<p>I am attaching a patch of pom.xml that resolves the issue for the master branch.</p>\n\n<p>Older releases (tags) can be affected too. Maybe there should be a notice to put the new repository to local .m2/settings.xml if you do not intend to update older tags.</p>",
